  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This 36-minute recording captures a February 25, 1996, performance by the Mountain Goats at the Tower in Bremen, Germany [1][2]. It is the fourth show in the archive’s collection for the band [2]. The set includes thirteen songs, with several appearing for the first time in the archive, including “The Monkey Song,” “Snow Crush Killing Song,” “Tollund Man,” and “Stars Fell On Alabama” [1][2]. Rare tracks such as “Orange Ball of Hate,” “The Hot Garden Stomp,” “Banter (Through the Mists of Time),” “Stars Around Her,” and “Tulsa Imperative” also feature in the lineup [1][2]. The uploader notes that “Seeing Daylight” was performed with a guest [1]. The recording was transferred by notasfarwest [1]. The setlist provided by the uploader lists “No, I Can’t” as the final song, though the official setlist data includes “Banter (Like a Bad Dog)” before it [1][2]. This is the only available recording of this specific show [1].",
